  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/plunge_depth_tab.rs` pins two cases. No production code changes.\n- `the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_pecks_its_tab_window_dives` (renamed from `the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_names_its_tab_window_dives`):\n  - The `2d/contour-tabs` case has no `PlungeTooDeep` finding.\n  - Four dive columns reach the last level. Each column stops at Z 4, Z 2 and Z 0.\n  - No step bites more than the 2 mm stepdown below the Z 6 stock top or below the depth before it.\n- `a_tabbed_contour_under_carried_stock_names_its_deep_dives` (new):\n  - The same case, with the contour top 4 mm under the stock top. The test sets it with `EditOperationParams`.\n  - The verifier names four dives. Each is a feed plunge that lands on Z 2 and bites 4 mm against the 2 mm stepdown.\n  - No finding holds the post.\n  - This keeps the #3679 law pinned end to end through the app (stepdown wiring, generate, cached warnings).\n- `docs/decisions/3925-plunge-tab-pin.md` records the choice.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #3847 (#3679) and PR #3866 (#3678) merged one minute apart. #3866 pecks the three tab window dives. The verifier then correctly names no dive. The test expectation from #3847 was out of date. The toolpath is correct.\n\n## Tests\n\nCommands on the final head `cfa62b88f`, against upstream/main `81365c33b`:\n\n- Before the change: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test plunge_depth_tab` failed: `three tab window dives named: [] left: 0 right: 3`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1 step, `app suites: plunge_depth_tab`, ok (2 passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\" --only \"app suites: example_catalog_adaptive\" --only \"app suites: example_catalog_edge_work\"`: 3 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: \"the diff reaches no heavy lane: nothing to run\".\n\nMutation checks (each reverted after the run):\n\n1. `contour_peck::peck_depths` returns `[z]` (no peck). `the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_pecks_its_tab_window_dives` fails: three `PlungeTooDeep` findings of 6 mm. Red.\n2. `sim::verify::plunge_depth` never pushes `PlungeTooDeep`. `a_tabbed_contour_under_carried_stock_names_its_deep_dives` fails: no finding. Red.\n\nWith the code restored, both tests pass.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc`, `.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changes. The three example catalog suites pass.\n\n## Found\n\nUnder carried stock, the first peck of a later tab window bites 4 mm. The #3678 floor (one stepdown over the first level) does not see the stock above the op top. The generator \"Carried stock\" note and the verifier both name it. Follow-up: #3926 (P7). The new test pins the current behaviour; a fix for #3926 changes it on purpose.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI display of the finding and the MCP `plunge_too_deep` mapping. This PR does not touch them.\n- Linux and Windows. The run was on macOS.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/app/tests/plunge_depth_tab.rs`.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3925\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
